```
Reason:
These statements assume that the MCP251x CAN controller will enter configuration mode within a fixed time after a reset. If the hardware takes longer than expected (5ms), the condition will fail, leading to premature failure detection and incorrect error reporting.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
timeout = jiffies + HZ;
while ((mcp251x_read_reg(spi, CANSTAT) & CANCTRL_REQOP_MASK) !=
       CANCTRL_REQOP_CONF) {
    usleep_range(MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000,
                 MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000 * 2);
    if (time_after(jiffies, timeout)) {
        dev_err(&spi->dev,
            "MCP251x didn't enter in conf mode after reset\n");
        return -EBUSY;
    }
}
```
Reason:
These statements implement a loop that continuously checks if the MCP251x has entered configuration mode, allowing for retries and a longer wait time. This accommodates variations in hardware response time, preventing premature failure detection and ensuring proper initialization of the device.

